##* {{RQ:Austen Emma|volume=I|chapter=II|text=''For a few days, every morning visit in Highbury included some mention of the '''handsome''' letter Mrs. Weston had received. “I suppose you have heard of the '''handsome''' letter Mr. Frank Churchill has written to Mrs. Weston? I understand it was a very '''handsome''' letter, indeed. Mr. Woodhouse told me of it. Mr. Woodhouse saw the letter, and he says he never saw such a '''handsome''' letter in his life.”''}}
